                "instructions": "Write a function `normalizePath(path)` that simplifies a Unix path containing '.' and '..' segments (e.g. `'/a/b/../c'` -> `'/a/c'`).",
                "starterCode": "function normalizePath(path) {\n  const parts = path.split('/');\n  const stack = [];\n  for (const part of parts) {\n    if (part === '' || part === '.') continue;\n    if (part === '..') {\n      if (stack.length > 0) stack.pop();\n    } else {\n      stack.push(part);\n    }\n  }\n  return '/' + stack.join('/');\n}",
